{"name":"Strawberry Milk","hex":"#ffd9e7","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"strawberry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The sweet, usually red, edible accessory fruit of certain plants of the genus Fragaria.","Any plant of the genus Fragaria (that bears such fruit)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing or having the flavor of strawberries.","Flavored with ethyl methylphenylglycidate, an artificial compound which is said to resemble the taste of strawberries."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strawberry"},{"term":"milk","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A white liquid produced by the mammary glands of female mammals to nourish their young. From certain animals, especially cows, it is also called dairy milk and is a common food for humans as a beverage or used to produce various dairy products such as butter, cheese, and yogurt.","A white (or whitish) liquid obtained from a vegetable source such as almonds, coconuts, oats, rice, or soy beans."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To express milk from (a mammal, especially a cow).","To draw (milk) from the breasts or udder."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/milk"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crayon Pop","blocks":[{"text":"Crayon Pop (Korean: 크레용팝) is a South Korean girl group formed under Chrome Entertainment in 2012. The group consisted of four members: Geummi, Ellin, Choa, and Way. Their fifth member, Soyul, left the group in 2017."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/%ED%81%AC%EB%A0%88%EC%9A%A9%ED%8C%9D%28Crayon_Pop%29_%EB%8F%84%EC%8B%9C_%EA%BC%AC%EB%A7%88%EB%93%A4%EC%9D%98_%ED%96%89%EB%B3%B5%ED%95%9C_%EC%B6%95%EC%A0%9C_%ED%8B%B0%EB%B8%8C%EB%A1%9C%EB%93%9C_%EC%9B%90%EC%9D%8C%EB%B0%A9%EC%86%A1_01.jpg/330px-%ED%81%AC%EB%A0%88%EC%9A%A9%ED%8C%9D%28Crayon_Pop%29_%EB%8F%84%EC%8B%9C_%EA%BC%AC%EB%A7%88%EB%93%A4%EC%9D%98_%ED%96%89%EB%B3%B5%ED%95%9C_%EC%B6%95%EC%A0%9C_%ED%8B%B0%EB%B8%8C%EB%A1%9C%EB%93%9C_%EC%9B%90%EC%9D%8C%EB%B0%A9%EC%86%A1_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crayon_Pop"},{"title":"Flavored milk","blocks":[{"text":"Flavored milk is a sweetened dairy drink made with milk, sugar, flavorings, and sometimes food colorings. It may be sold as a pasteurized, refrigerated product, or as an ultra-high-temperature (UHT) treated product not requiring refrigeration. It may also be made in restaurants or homes by mixing flavorings into milk."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Binggrae_Banana_Flavored_Milk_03.jpg/330px-Binggrae_Banana_Flavored_Milk_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flavored_milk"},{"title":"Strawberry","blocks":[{"text":"The garden strawberry is a widely grown hybrid plant cultivated worldwide for its fruit. The genus Fragaria, the strawberries, is in the rose family, Rosaceae. The fruit is appreciated for its aroma, bright red colour, juicy texture, and sweetness. It is eaten either fresh or in prepared foods such as jam, ice cream, and chocolates. Artificial strawberry flavourings and aromas are widely used in commercial products. Botanically, the strawberry is not a berry, but an aggregate accessory fruit. Each apparent 'seed' on the outside of the strawberry is actually an achene, a botanical fruit with a seed inside it."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Garden_strawberry_%28Fragaria_%C3%97_ananassa%29_single2.jpg/330px-Garden_strawberry_%28Fragaria_%C3%97_ananassa%29_single2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strawberry"},{"title":"Milk","blocks":[{"text":"Milk is usually a white liquid food produced by the mammary glands of lactating mammals. It is the primary source of nutrition for young mammals before they are able to digest solid food. Milk contains many nutrients, including calcium and protein, as well as lactose and saturated fat; the enzyme lactase is needed to break down lactose. Immune factors and immune-modulating components in milk contribute to milk immunity. The first milk, which is called colostrum, contains antibodies and immune-modulating components that strengthen the immune system against many diseases."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Glass_of_Milk_%2833657535532%29.jpg/330px-Glass_of_Milk_%2833657535532%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milk"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/%ED%81%AC%EB%A0%88%EC%9A%A9%ED%8C%9D_2012_%EC%84%9C%EC%9A%B8_DMC%EC%BB%AC%EC%B2%98%EC%98%A4%ED%94%88_%ED%8A%B9%EB%B3%84%EA%B3%B5%EA%B0%9C%EB%B0%A9%EC%86%A1_%EC%86%90%EB%B0%94%EB%8B%A5TV.jpg/500px-%ED%81%AC%EB%A0%88%EC%9A%A9%ED%8C%9D_2012_%EC%84%9C%EC%9A%B8_DMC%EC%BB%AC%EC%B2%98%EC%98%A4%ED%94%88_%ED%8A%B9%EB%B3%84%EA%B3%B5%EA%B0%9C%EB%B0%A9%EC%86%A1_%EC%86%90%EB%B0%94%EB%8B%A5TV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/%ED%81%AC%EB%A0%88%EC%9A%A9%ED%8C%9D_2012_%EC%84%9C%EC%9A%B8_DMC%EC%BB%AC%EC%B2%98%EC%98%A4%ED%94%88_%ED%8A%B9%EB%B3%84%EA%B3%B5%EA%B0%9C%EB%B0%A9%EC%86%A1_%EC%86%90%EB%B0%94%EB%8B%A5TV.jpg/500px-%ED%81%AC%EB%A0%88%EC%9A%A9%ED%8C%9D_2012_%EC%84%9C%EC%9A%B8_DMC%EC%BB%AC%EC%B2%98%EC%98%A4%ED%94%88_%ED%8A%B9%EB%B3%84%EA%B3%B5%EA%B0%9C%EB%B0%A9%EC%86%A1_%EC%86%90%EB%B0%94%EB%8B%A5TV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Crayon Pop performing \"Saturday Night\" in September 2012","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A%ED%81%AC%EB%A0%88%EC%9A%A9%ED%8C%9D_2012_%EC%84%9C%EC%9A%B8_DMC%EC%BB%AC%EC%B2%98%EC%98%A4%ED%94%88_%ED%8A%B9%EB%B3%84%EA%B3%B5%EA%B0%9C%EB%B0%A9%EC%86%A1_%EC%86%90%EB%B0%94%EB%8B%A5TV.jpg"